The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;e Reasonable Exception Statement; Arboricultural Impact
Assessment; Envirosearch Residential; Flood Risk Assessment; Location Plan; Site
Plan (NGL 696783); Reasonable Exception Statement; 01; 02; 03; 04; 05; 06; 07; 08;
09; 10; 11 Rev A; 12 Rev A; 13 Rev A; 14; 15; 16 Rev B; 17 Rev C; 18.&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The development of any buildings hereby permitted shall not
be commenced until works for the disposal of surface water have been submitted
to, and approved in writing by, the local planning authority.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The development shall be undertaken in accordance with the approved details and thereafter retained.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The development of any building hereby permitted shall not
be&amp;nbsp;commenced until Flood Mitigation Measures have been submitted to and
approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.&amp;nbsp; The applicant should provide detailed description of building materials, foundations, floor, wall, fittings, services, doors and windows that minimise water entry whilst maintaining structural integrity, materials and construction techniques that facilitate drying and cleaning, in line with &#x27;Improving the Flood Performance of New Buildings&#x27; publication taking into account the expected depth of flooding.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The development shall be undertaken in accordance with the approved details and thereafter retained.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
